WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.280
On an ancient battlefield,
two armies face each other.

2
00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:07.870
One warrior refuses to
fight his own relatives.

3
00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:12.910
In the Bhagavad Gita, Krishna tells him that
a warrior's duty is to fight a righteous

4
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.080
war.

5
00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:17.910
Centuries later, Gandhi, the
great champion of non-violence,

6
00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:20.760
called the same book his guide.

7
00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:26.190
How can one book call a man to battle,
and still guide a man of peace?

8
00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:28.810
In this mission, you'll
meet the warrior's duty,

9
00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:32.630
and the Gita's teaching that
the soul cannot be killed.

10
00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:35.780
Then you'll explore what
Gandhi meant by non-violence,

11
00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:38.530
and weigh up whether it can work today.

12
00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:43.800
Your mission: explain how one book can
call a warrior to fight and still guide

13
00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:45.540
a champion of non-violence.
